{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-pi/src/project.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:01:07.790076Z","id":"6fb75516687443d8a41e71ad1798d984a9b2ed30c46621c25782440d8bb88c9f","body":{"detail":"In the Pi reader (src/provider.rs) Entry::Compaction becomes a System Item::Turn, and the loop here discards Item::Event. Walking items instead of turns() changes nothing. A compaction turn projects as a plain System message, not an Entry::Compaction, because pi_extras always returns None (so the emit_compaction this diff deletes was never reached on main either). The comment describes a design that this branch backed out (commit 5076cc4).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":163},"end":{"line":172},"content_hash":"1f4b2d739bf7eda400de7a5d8fae7a5f92fa4ba2e1ef4908d73c1abaab1e777a"},"suggested_fix":"Loop over view.turns() and change the comment to say events are dropped and a compaction turn projects as a System message.","summary":"Pi project_view's comment says it walks view.items so compaction boundaries land between the surrounding turns, but Pi compaction is a Turn and every Item::Event is dropped","tags":["review","review:pr-144-qual-3"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-pi/src/project.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:08:39.606097Z","id":"7df263dd7f95ba61584b53bcf1addcade7c79bfa752d6688bbb347a74b41ffb8","body":{"detail":"crates/toolpath-pi/src/project.rs:163-172: the loop ignores Item::Event. crates/toolpath-pi/src/provider.rs:255-262 reads Entry::Compaction as Item::Turn with Role::System. pi_extras (project.rs:186-188) always returns None. The output is the same as walking view.turns(), which origin/main project.rs:165 did, so only the new comment is wrong.","kind":"comment","references":"6fb75516687443d8a41e71ad1798d984a9b2ed30c46621c25782440d8bb88c9f","summary":"confirmed: regression in the comment: Pi project_view says it walks items so compaction boundaries land in place, but Pi compaction is a Turn and every Item::Event is dropped","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-pi/src/project.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:11:45.659362Z","id":"78dd6c891a56f0b8c255a25300db2a314192508d7b24be986ca0c45a25ff0c3e","body":{"detail":"Failure: test-fixtures/claude/convo.jsonl through toolpath_claude::provider::to_view and PiProjector gives 67 entries, 7 of whose parentId values name no entry (claude-headerless-1, claude-headerless-2, claude-headerless-4, the attachment 768a7ebf-..., claude-headerless-6, ...). test-fixtures/codex/convo.jsonl through toolpath_codex::to_view and PiProjector gives 10 entries, 5 with a dangling parentId (task_started-..., turn_context-..., agent_message-...). I checked both with a throwaway test on this branch. Cause: the Claude reader (crates/toolpath-claude/src/provider.rs, conversation_to_view) now chains turns onto headerless and message-less events, and the Codex reader chains every item onto the item before it, events included. base_for and the assistant branch of emit_turn_entries copy turn.parent_id into EntryBase.parent_id, but the loop at line 165 skips Item::Event, so the named parent is never written. On origin/main the Claude reader redirected message-less entries to the previous turn and never chained through headerless lines, and the Codex chain was synthesized over turns only, so Pi received parents that existed. Pi stores a session as a tree keyed by parentId and rebuilds context by walking parents from the leaf, so a dangling parent cuts the resumed context at that entry. The cross-harness matrix does not catch it because parent_id_graph compares two passes through the same harness and resolves parents past events.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":163},"end":{"line":173},"content_hash":"e017c69af5bcacaeeac3d3fddfa424fef29cd6b70556c58b20cf6eee32b0ca44"},"suggested_fix":"In Pi project_view, build an id -> parent_id map of every Item::Event (as the Claude projector's wire_parent does for headerless events) and resolve each turn's parent_id past events before writing it; add a matrix or Pi test asserting every projected parentId names an entry in the projected session.","summary":"Pi project_view drops every Item::Event but still writes each turn's parent_id verbatim, so exporting a Claude or Codex session to Pi now produces entries whose parentId names an entry that is not in the file","tags":["review","review:pr-144-qual-3","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-pi/src/project.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:11:45.659444Z","id":"0a2ff40891b7e4110fea433bb8d2808ea3a999633eb2df5a2e6be4f02875aaa6","body":{"detail":"emit_turn_entries writes toolResult entries chained after the assistant (`<turn>-tr-<n>`, parent = previous entry), but nothing redirects the following turn: its parentId is turn.parent_id, which for a Claude source is the assistant uuid (the reader maps an absorbed carrier's uuid to the assistant turn). The result is assistant -> {toolResult chain, next turn}. Walking parents from Pi's leaf skips every toolResult, so a resumed session shows tool calls with no results. The Claude projector solves the same problem with parent_rewrites (crates/toolpath-claude/src/project.rs, the Role::Assistant arm).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":316},"end":{"line":375},"content_hash":"4630536cde2fac64fc9520e7cccb1ed39282817dbd5b0f1cd3ef2d2da681dc9b"},"suggested_fix":"Track, per assistant turn id, the id of the last toolResult entry emitted for it, and when writing a later turn whose parent_id names that assistant, use the last toolResult id instead.","summary":"Pre-existing on main: Pi project_view parents the next turn on the assistant entry, not on its last toolResult entry, so the tool results it writes are a side branch off the conversation path","tags":["review","review:pr-144-qual-3","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-pi/src/project.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:16:43.367438Z","id":"ba8a00a15a10c83e88e856c126654557fcdd26ddf7470f3f50d9318a9ef44986","body":{"detail":"crates/toolpath-pi/src/project.rs:163-172 (Item::Event(_) => {}) and emit_assistant writing turn.parent_id unchanged. Throwaway test (to_view + PiProjector, entries serialized, parentId checked against ids): this branch, Claude fixture 7 dangling (claude-headerless-1, -2, -4, 768a7ebf-..., claude-headerless-6, e797831d-..., 3eb41279-...), Codex fixture 5 dangling (task_started-..., turn_context-..., agent_message-...). Same test on an origin/main snapshot with identical fixtures: 0 dangling for both.","kind":"comment","references":"78dd6c891a56f0b8c255a25300db2a314192508d7b24be986ca0c45a25ff0c3e","summary":"confirmed: regression - Pi project_view skips Item::Event but copies turn.parent_id as is, so Claude and Codex fixtures exported to Pi get parentIds that name no entry","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-pi/src/project.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:16:43.367467Z","id":"756af11faa3bb1d52d987c64cb08ff1d09c4ad1d8bc5186afe00ba63bc4a9b7c","body":{"detail":"emit_assistant (crates/toolpath-pi/src/project.rs:355-374) chains <turn>-tr-<n> after the assistant, and the next turn keeps turn.parent_id (the assistant). Throwaway test on test-fixtures/claude/convo.jsonl -> to_view -> PiProjector: 19 toolResult entries, 19 with no entry naming them as parent; identical 19/19 on an origin/main snapshot. Concern is the right kind for a pre-existing Pi issue.","kind":"comment","references":"0a2ff40891b7e4110fea433bb8d2808ea3a999633eb2df5a2e6be4f02875aaa6","summary":"confirmed: pre-existing on main - every toolResult entry Pi project_view writes has no child, so the next turn hangs off the assistant and the tool results sit on a side branch","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-pi/src/project.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T20:44:28.514515Z","id":"71e6d32403b32ac93a8c2a6d884520a3ed3be3db0593828b159accf8146dc68b","body":{"detail":"Owner decision, 2026-10-13. The alternative (turns chain turn-to-turn, events hang off the preceding turn as leaves) was considered and rejected: it would make every event a fork and a dead end to any DAG reader, and dead ends in Toolpath carry a semantic meaning, abandoned work, that events would pollute. So the linear chain through events is the model, and the export breakage it causes is this PR's to fix: one generic helper in the shared layer that maps a parent id to the nearest ancestor the target harness keeps, used by Pi and any other projector that skips events (see also 5dcb8531 for the Claude projector's handling of foreign event types, and b635ad3c for the matrix test).","kind":"decision","references":"78dd6c891a56f0b8c255a25300db2a314192508d7b24be986ca0c45a25ff0c3e","summary":"Decided: the event chain stays. Events are steps on the main line, turns may parent events, and dead ends keep their meaning (abandoned work). Consequence: a projector to a harness that drops events must resolve each parent past the dropped events, and the cross-harness matrix must catch a dangling parent after the first leg","tags":["review:pr-144-qual-3","decision","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-pi/src/project.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T20:47:25.457177Z","id":"6b4c08f02da2ef91ce409f4f0136a3f5c4c99ceba6a8b71b89474a6aac928900","body":{"detail":"Owner approval, 2026-10-13. Text written by this PR; rides along in the #144 fix pass.","kind":"decision","references":"6fb75516687443d8a41e71ad1798d984a9b2ed30c46621c25782440d8bb88c9f","suggested_fix":"Loop over view.turns() and change the comment to say events are dropped and a compaction turn projects as a System message.","summary":"Decided: fix as suggested (text this PR wrote)","tags":["review:pr-144-qual-3","decision","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-pi/src/project.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T21:04:24.786003Z","id":"2aae19bc81ba78a7dafb2836e57ff847d19765125565e86464a19f1364d014d2","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:97e1b9b","summary":"Fixed in 97e1b9b on ben/items-ir: KeptAncestors (toolpath-convo) resolves a parent past dropped items; the Pi projector writes resolved parents. Evidence: toolpath-pi test_turn_parent_resolves_past_dropped_events passes, and the matrix assertion from 56da06a passes for claude->pi and codex->pi but fails (7 and 4 dangling) against the pre-fix Pi projector. Other projectors (codex, copilot, cursor, gemini, opencode) write no IR parent ids, so they do not share the bug.","supersedes":"78dd6c891a56f0b8c255a25300db2a314192508d7b24be986ca0c45a25ff0c3e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
